  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "NvEncSharp 2.2.0 fixes encoding, decoding, color conversion, and native interop issues. (BREAKING CHANGE)\n\nBreaking changes\n- Removed NvEncRegisterResourceEx.AsInputPointer() and .AsOutputPointer(). Registered resource handles must be mapped with NvEncoder.MapInputResource() before encoding. Use the returned MappedResource and MappedBufferFmt, then unmap before unregistering. For bitstream output, use NvEncoder.CreateBitstreamBuffer().\n- Changed LibCuVideo.GetDecodeStatus()'s output parameter to CuVideoGetDecodeStatus, matching the native API and fixing a potential memory corruption issue. The CuVideoDecoder.GetDecodeStatus() wrapper still returns CuVideoDecodeStatus.\n\nLibrary fixes\n- Fixed generated bitfield accessors, including masks, offsets, and signed values, and regenerated the affected structures.\n- Fixed CuVideoFormat.VideoFormat and VideoFullRange bit accessors.\n- Corrected NV_ENC_CREATE_INPUT_BUFFER_VER for input buffer creation.\n- Fixed missing structure versions in GetEncodePresetConfig(). Marked its overloads obsolete; use GetEncodePresetConfigEx() for P1-P7 presets.\n- Fixed NAL packet parsing when data precedes a start code.\n- Fixed CUDA color conversion that truncated pixel values, including incorrect RGB24 packing. Updated the bundled native DLL.\n\nSample fixes\n- Fixed screen capture encoding to use mapped resources and release them in the correct order.\n- Restored decoded frame copies to host memory.\n- Fixed video playback timing and frame queuing, with a 30 FPS fallback when timing metadata is unavailable.\n- Fixed buffered NAL submission and end-of-stream flushing.\n- Added explicit rejection of unsupported video formats in the decoding sample, which supports 8-bit 4:2:0 H.264 with NV12 output.\n- Improved decoding sample shutdown and resource cleanup.\n\nAdded Windows x64 native structure size and field offset validation, and expanded NAL parsing tests.",
